XDJ-RX: USB on the i.MX6 ChipIdea host controllers.

  - dev-hub.c: a USB 2.0 (high-speed) hub descriptor, so the hub can sit on the
    high-speed-only EHCI root port like the real HOST1 hub; report
    PORT_STAT_HIGH_SPEED for high-speed devices.
  - chipidea.c: OTG VBUS-valid; mark the controller TDI-style (tdi).
  - hcd-ehci.c/.h, hcd-ehci-sysbus.c (TDI/ChipIdea only): PORTSC[27:26] PSPD port
    speed (Linux reads it; without it everything enumerated at 12 Mbit/s);
    USBSTS[7] SRI reads 1 (the i.MX6 BSP busy-waits on it for high-speed links);
    re-poll the async schedule every microframe while busy (5 ms window).
Result: the front slots run at 480 Mbit/s; with the macOS timer fix USB reads go
from 1.3 to ~5.5 MB/s. (Replaces the old patches 08, 12 and 20.)

